            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "robgraphics"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added the thyme to the broth to insfuse the flavor instead of sprinkling it on the top at the end. Used an immersion blender to somewhat smooth out the soup. I was tempted to add a half cup of cream but very glad I didn't. The Asiago gave the soup such a great, tangy taste and creamy richness.\nIf you want a thicker soup, just add a tablespoon of cornstarch mixed with some cold water.\nPerfect, fast and simple soup. I will be making this again, in spite of my wife not liking Asiago or Rosemary.",
            "datePublished": "2022-01-11T22:39:35.693Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Even my son, who won't eat cauliflower, loves this soup. The only tweaks I made were to roast the garlic and cauliflower at 400 before adding to the soup. This extra step added a LOT of flavor. I also discovered that changing the cheese added dimension. One time, I used Bellavita brand asiago and it was a definite game changer.",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-18T01:12:02.430Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SweetTreat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is a keeper. I did change a few things around...I used a 32 oz Box of Chicken Broth to boil Cauliflower in, but after accessing everything ink re I wanted thicker soup so I then took 8oz of Broth out the pot before putting the cheese mix in. Also, you don’t really need the fresh herbs...I moved around my weekly food budget thinking I needed them and I didn’t, but it was a nice touch. Overall, I loved and the cauliflower as cheese mix great beginning to a roast or mashed cauliflower “potato” dish!",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-09T21:45:24.290Z"
          },
